The mechanism and regression scenario are clear, but an observable difference requires a particular hook-list state and overlapping submission timing. The supplied diff does not show whether or how often those runtime conditions occur in real applications.

React's form-transition hook initialization now distinguishes a fully upgraded form fiber from one that merely has a single existing hook. The accompanying focused test targets two rapid submissions while the first asynchronous form action is still pending and expects both actions to run without an exception.

Likely behavioral changes
  • When a form fiber has one existing state hook but no following hook, it is no longer treated as already fully stateful. This is intended to let two closely spaced submissions of the same form both invoke the asynchronous form action without throwing; the regression test observes two action invocations.

